{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAFmQtfUrCCAGdStQpGh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The fix is written and the tests pass, but I couldn't commit it because this repo has no git author identity set. The changes are uncommitted on a new branch, `fix/recover-abort-handler`.\n\n**Change (`recovery.go`):** the recovery middleware now handles a panic with `http.ErrAbortHandler` the same way it already handles a broken connection, and that includes wrapped errors. It:\n- logs a one-line message with the request dump, but no `[Recovery] … panic recovered` stack trace;\n- records the error with `c.Error` and calls `c.Abort()`;\n- does not write a 500 and does not call the recovery handler.\n\n**Test (`recovery_test.go`):** I added `TestPanicWithAbortHandler`. It checks that the status the handler had already set is kept, that the log contains the abort error, and that the log has no stack-trace header. `go test ./...` and `go vet` pass.\n\n**Your call:** I chose to absorb the panic, which is what \"suppress\" asks for. The other option is to re-panic so that `net/http` itself drops the connection, which is what this sentinel is normally for. With the current change the connection is not forcibly closed; any response already started just ends normally. I can switch it to re-panic if you want that behaviour.\n\nTo commit, set your identity (`git config user.name/user.email`) and run `git commit -am \"fix(recover): suppress http.ErrAbortHandler in recover\"`. Or tell me the identity to use and I'll commit it."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":349,"cache_read_input_tokens":34364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":349,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba8b0aaa-8f06-4ff4-8527-51f8c7ee1a79","uuid":"c753f163-68b5-4da5-9892-aed165c6d846","timestamp":"2026-10-18T19:28:58.380Z","request_id":"req_011CgAFmQgGLHTBcAemhkGj3"}
